// M1 root cause (net/http_resp_parse.oo:79-85, committed 2026-09-02):
//     let rest: String = str_slice(line, colon + 1, chars_len(line));
//     let rlen: Int = chars_len(rest);
//     let mut val: String = rest;                  // moves `rest`
//     if rlen > 0 {
//         if char_at(rest, 0) == " " {             // USE AFTER MOVE
//             val = str_slice(rest, 1, rlen);      // second use
// The checker's move analysis is correct — String moves, `rest` is
// dead after line 81. Fix shape: slice the space first, or bind
// `val` from a second slice of `line`. This is the kind of defect
// the type system exists to catch; the file predates the check.

// m1 (masked): net/ANCHOR.oo:122 `net_mod_tcp_read(tcp, fd)` calls
// net_tcp_read with 2 args; uncommitted net/tcp.oo:31-36 requires 3.
// Will surface as an arity error once M1 is fixed. Update the wrapper
// in the same commit as the tcp.oo signature change.

